<DocsPageSectionTitle>
    Best Practices
</DocsPageSectionTitle>

<DocsPageSubsectionTitle IncludeInToc="false">
    Content Hierarchy
</DocsPageSubsectionTitle>

<DocsPageParagraph>
    Dividers should separate related groups rather than compensate for an unclear page structure. Prefer spacing or semantic headings whenever they communicate the relationship between sections more clearly.
</DocsPageParagraph>

<DocsPageSubsectionTitle IncludeInToc="false">
    Subtle Separation
</DocsPageSubsectionTitle>

<DocsPageParagraph>
    Decorative dividers should not compete with the content they organize. When a divider contains text, keep the label concise and preserve the document's semantic heading structure separately.
</DocsPageParagraph>

